From 6119bcf487fcb9651dcb160e7c960abbc5fb0ea6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:19:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: add back to top CMS component

Add BackToTopComponent (cx-back-to-top), mapped to the
BackToTopComponent CMS type. The component renders a floating button
once the page is scrolled beyond a display threshold, which defaults to
400px and can be configured globally (backToTop.displayThreshold) or
per component through the CMS data.

- scroll events are listened to outside the Angular zone and audited,
  so change detection only runs when the visibility changes
- the scroll listener is removed when the component is destroyed
- clicking the button scrolls smoothly to the top (instant when the
  user prefers reduced motion) and moves the focus to the start of the
  document, so keyboard users continue from the top of the page
- the button is a native, labelled button element
